# Example: Excel Extension Commands
# Demonstrates the new Excel-specific DSL extension commands
#
# Prerequisites:
# - Microsoft Excel must be installed
# - Accessibility permissions must be granted
#
# Commands used:
# - range A1       - Navigate to cell A1
# - range A1:B5    - Select range A1:B5
# - typeincell A1 "text" - Type into cell A1
# - getcell A1     - Read value from cell A1
# - getcell A1 as varname - Read value and store in variable

launch Excel
wait 3

# Create a new blank workbook
find Blank Workbook
click
wait 2

log Starting Excel extension demo...

# Navigate to and type in cells
typeincell A1 "Name"
typeincell B1 "Score"
typeincell A2 "Alice"
typeincell B2 "95"
typeincell A3 "Bob"
typeincell B3 "87"
typeincell A4 "Charlie"
typeincell B4 "92"

# Navigate to a specific cell
range B5

# Type a formula (note: formulas start with =)
typeincell B5 "=SUM(B2:B4)"

# Read back the calculated total
getcell B5 as total

log Excel extension demo complete!
log Check the spreadsheet for the results
